WEBVTT

00:04.551 --> 00:08.559
Andy and Fuko.
There's something I'd like you two to investigate.

00:08.893 --> 00:10.897
Aye! You can count on me, please!

00:11.314 --> 00:14.070
I want you to check the legitimacy
of a certain book.

00:14.487 --> 00:15.280
A book?

00:17.368 --> 00:20.708
There is a chance that the pages
of the book in question hold...

00:20.708 --> 00:25.175
...the past and future events of this world
as penned by a certain Artifact.

00:25.927 --> 00:31.020
Since Billy has rebelled,
not even I know the route from here on out.

00:31.522 --> 00:37.534
To clear these four Quests in this unfamiliar situation,
that book will be paramount.

00:37.867 --> 00:40.247
The past and future put down in...

00:41.040 --> 00:42.209
...a book?

00:42.418 --> 00:46.426
B-But, should we be handling such
an important mission?

00:46.885 --> 00:49.516
I would prefer if you both handle it, in fact.

00:52.396 --> 00:54.066
Once you see it,
the reason will be clear.

00:55.611 --> 00:56.362
This is it.

01:01.832 --> 01:05.130
<i>The Union has taken a huge blow from Billy's betrayal.</i>

01:05.130 --> 01:07.761
<i>Juiz gathers the bewildered members
of the Roundtable,</i>

01:07.761 --> 01:11.225
<i>and starts to speak the truth about
this world and her own situation.</i>

01:11.560 --> 01:15.985
<i>By God's hands, this world endlessly repeats destruction
and reconstruction.</i>

01:15.985 --> 01:20.536
<i>Juiz has been using an Artifact called Ark
to experience these Loops over and over.</i>

01:20.536 --> 01:26.214
<i>One other, Victor, has also been living
within multiple Loops with his Undead ability.</i>

01:26.632 --> 01:32.142
<i>Fuko sees an eternal solitude from the truth
where he cannot die even at the world's end.</i>

01:32.727 --> 01:37.111
<i>Juiz declares the only ways to escape
the Rules are suicide or God-slaying,</i>

01:37.111 --> 01:41.411
<i>and bows down in apology for hiding the truth
and using all of her comrades.</i>

01:41.995 --> 01:45.460
<i>However, the members of the Roundtable
did not want an apology from her.</i>

01:45.837 --> 01:50.053
<i>Under Juiz who wants to slay God and liberate
the world from irrational rules,</i>

01:50.053 --> 01:52.349
<i>the comrades unify once again.</i>

01:52.349 --> 01:58.069
And the item she pulls out as an undertaking
for their comeback surprises Fuko.

02:01.827 --> 02:05.501
Th-That's the book I use as my life's bible...

02:05.626 --> 02:11.972
...the masterpiece by Anno Un-sensei,
who holds the longest-running shojo manga record!

02:13.266 --> 02:16.648
Known as You-Me!

02:17.191 --> 02:18.234
Right.

02:18.611 --> 02:19.696
And...

02:22.409 --> 02:27.629
This is from Volume 20 of You-Me,
the Space Soccer Club Invasion arc.

02:27.879 --> 02:33.348
The Space Soccer Club is about to blow up
the entire school, but the team captain's...

02:33.808 --> 02:35.937
Spiral Shot of Justice!

02:36.270 --> 02:40.028
...destroys all the goals and restores peace.

02:40.696 --> 02:43.619
Doesn't this story sound familiar?

02:54.056 --> 02:55.768
I'll just have to...

02:55.768 --> 02:57.062
...negate that justice.

03:06.205 --> 03:07.709
The aliens from the other day!

03:09.754 --> 03:10.631
In addition...

03:12.384 --> 03:18.814
The Rotten High School Melee arc in volumes 11
to 18 can look like a prediction of the Spoil battle.

03:20.901 --> 03:22.362
We need to investigate.

03:25.620 --> 03:26.495
Question, Boss!

03:26.913 --> 03:28.499
Yes, Top?

03:28.499 --> 03:33.051
Are you being for real?
Uh, also, what's this You-Me thing?

03:33.259 --> 03:35.096
Are you saying you don't know, Top?

03:35.096 --> 03:37.935
You-Me is only the gold standard
of long-running sci-fi shojo manga!

03:38.102 --> 03:40.858
It's got battles, too,
so even you can read it, Top.

03:41.233 --> 03:42.612
There's 101 volumes in all!

03:42.612 --> 03:44.073
101?

03:45.576 --> 03:49.291
But no one knows anything beyond the manga.

03:49.751 --> 03:52.464
There's no info about the author at all.

03:52.464 --> 03:53.634
That is correct.

03:53.967 --> 04:00.105
If You-Me was drawn with the Artifact G-Liner
as I predict...

04:00.438 --> 04:05.574
the objects drawn themselves
are not affected by the addition of new Rules.

04:05.825 --> 04:09.164
In other words, the raw manuscript
doesn't fall under the language unification,

04:09.164 --> 04:10.668
and will still be in Japanese.

04:11.168 --> 04:12.045
Right.

04:13.089 --> 04:14.383
The raw manuscript...

04:16.220 --> 04:17.724
Andy, Fuko.

04:18.433 --> 04:20.563
There are two things I want you to look into.

04:20.813 --> 04:26.449
I want the status of the raw manuscript
and intel on the author, Anno Un.

04:27.242 --> 04:28.829
I'll leave the means up to you.

04:29.329 --> 04:32.503
If those two are anywhere,
it would be at the publisher.

04:32.503 --> 04:35.341
But I doubt they'll show it to us just like that.

04:35.341 --> 04:36.678
Which means...

04:40.018 --> 04:41.605
So amazing...

04:43.525 --> 04:46.363
...all we gotta do is whip up
a killer manga and bring it to 'em, right?

04:46.698 --> 04:48.994
- What?
- What?

06:20.426 --> 06:22.138
2020

06:22.138 --> 06:24.184
DECEMBER 3RD

06:24.184 --> 06:29.194
UNDEAD + UNLUCK

06:50.069 --> 06:51.906
Pappy said you can use this room!

06:57.042 --> 06:58.503
Thanks.

06:58.503 --> 07:02.218
While I'm puttin' ya out,
ya mind preparin' the stuff on this list?

07:02.720 --> 07:03.680
Aye, aye!

07:14.744 --> 07:18.000
Urgh... urrrgh...

07:20.296 --> 07:21.758
What're ya stressing about?

07:21.800 --> 07:25.348
This is impossible!
Why am I the one making it?

07:25.599 --> 07:28.855
I'm just a blissful connoisseur of fiction!

07:28.855 --> 07:31.235
There's a huge difference between being
a reader and a writer!

07:31.694 --> 07:33.280
I'll handle wrappin' it up.

07:33.489 --> 07:34.241
Huh?

07:35.326 --> 07:37.080
Okay, Unigle.

07:41.463 --> 07:44.929
Your basic manga pipeline looks somethin' like this.

07:45.848 --> 07:47.768
Andy, you've made a manga before?

07:48.227 --> 07:53.445
Not from scratch, no. But I dabbled a little
when Tezuka was hypin' up the manga industry.

07:53.613 --> 07:54.657
Tezu-

07:54.657 --> 07:57.580
SELF-CENSORED

08:02.548 --> 08:06.054
Composition, background art-
I got all that covered.

08:06.556 --> 08:08.768
But the base for it all.

08:10.354 --> 08:15.239
Now that's a spot where the passion
from your soul weighs in. Nobody can help you there.

08:17.578 --> 08:20.792
But you're the one with the most shojo manga know-how.

08:21.418 --> 08:26.971
So, ya just gotta dream up a boyfriend and situations
with him that'd make your heart throb to death!

08:29.184 --> 08:31.355
Can y'manage that, Fuko?

08:34.737 --> 08:35.864
Yeah!

08:40.916 --> 08:43.755
Well, you sure are takin' this in stride.

08:43.755 --> 08:46.218
I was expectin' ya to get
far more embarrassed than that.

08:46.218 --> 08:51.144
I can't afford to do that!
I don't want my shyness to cause any hangups.

08:51.688 --> 08:52.523
And besides...

08:53.733 --> 08:56.781
If You-Me really is a book of prophecies...

08:57.031 --> 09:00.371
...then its pages just might hold the key
to stopping Mr. Billy and his group.

09:01.624 --> 09:03.335
Doing it for Tatiana, huh?

09:03.335 --> 09:08.095
Of course that's one reason,
but if I can do a good job on this manga...

09:08.680 --> 09:12.437
...I think I'll be able
to understand my own feelings better.

09:13.397 --> 09:15.902
And if I can do that, then...

09:17.280 --> 09:20.871
...I'll be able to summon even stronger strokes of unluck!

09:24.795 --> 09:27.718
Right. That should be quite the treat.

09:42.246 --> 09:42.998
Well?

09:43.290 --> 09:47.173
I-I actually don't want you reading
it too carefully in detail.

09:51.473 --> 09:53.812
Sick. Wicked sick, in fact!

09:58.237 --> 10:00.408
Gonna compose the storyboard now!

10:00.408 --> 10:04.040
I'll have it done in an hour.
Everyone get ready to draw!

10:04.165 --> 10:05.251
Everyone?

10:05.794 --> 10:07.255
Shk-ping!

10:07.255 --> 10:09.718
Um, we're here. Per your request.

10:10.177 --> 10:11.764
It's Mui! And Mico!

10:12.056 --> 10:14.729
Um, if there's anything I can do to help-

10:14.770 --> 10:18.193
Go pump some iron.
Your power's too dangerous.

10:18.360 --> 10:19.572
Roger...

10:22.160 --> 10:24.164
Pan-Panda!

10:24.665 --> 10:27.336
But a manga takes a lot
of time to make!

10:27.462 --> 10:28.923
Not an issue.

10:29.424 --> 10:31.136
Mico! Get the gear I asked for.

10:31.136 --> 10:31.971
Aye, aye, sir!

10:33.348 --> 10:34.518
Gatch-ching!

10:35.770 --> 10:38.192
Whoa! They're moving on their own!

10:38.651 --> 10:44.204
With these brain wave-operated robot arms,
we'll finish up six times as fast.

10:44.204 --> 10:45.456
Brute force?

10:49.965 --> 10:52.805
But I can't control them at all!

10:52.805 --> 10:55.392
Yeah, I know.
That's why I'm givin' ya an hour.

10:56.311 --> 10:56.979
Get used to 'em.

10:57.063 --> 10:58.608
You can't be serious!

10:59.067 --> 11:02.240
APOLOGIES FOR THE INCONVENIENCE

11:11.174 --> 11:13.345
Imagine looking down at yourself from above.

11:14.765 --> 11:18.146
Once you get the hang of it,
the rest is a piece of cake.

11:18.480 --> 11:20.109
Oh, Tatiana!

11:20.401 --> 11:22.990
Time for training, Fuko!

11:35.682 --> 11:36.976
Fuko.

11:37.644 --> 11:42.194
Tatiana, thank you for giving me the drill!

11:42.194 --> 11:44.783
Of course I did.
We're friends.

11:45.451 --> 11:47.748
Thanks to you,
I can move these around now!

11:48.040 --> 11:52.633
Mm... I want to help out with this manga, too.

11:52.883 --> 11:55.346
You'll have less space to work with, but...

11:55.513 --> 11:58.143
You're more than welcome aboard!
Let's work together!

11:58.770 --> 12:00.022
The storyboard's done!

12:00.230 --> 12:01.024
That was fast!

12:01.984 --> 12:03.863
Pan-Panda!

13:22.604 --> 13:25.610
THE SWORD AND ZEN AS ONE

13:33.166 --> 13:34.168
I'll assist.

13:34.753 --> 13:35.880
Appreciate it.

13:40.807 --> 13:45.567
When you said it was a book of prophecies,
I went back and re-read You-Me again...

13:46.025 --> 13:52.162
But there was nothing in it that suggested
Mr. Billy's betrayal or our current set of quests.

13:52.956 --> 13:56.589
Instead there were these awkward gaps.

13:57.172 --> 14:01.932
The closer I got to the climax,
the more apparent the plot holes became.

14:02.474 --> 14:07.611
Even back when I was reading each chapter as it came out,
I'd often wonder if I somehow skipped a part.

14:10.032 --> 14:13.915
In other words... you believe
the author intentionally left parts out?

14:14.165 --> 14:14.875
That's my guess.

14:17.046 --> 14:19.801
We need to confirm that aspect of this as well.

14:20.637 --> 14:22.933
Which frame do you want me to help next-

14:23.475 --> 14:24.226
Hmm?

14:26.899 --> 14:29.780
Pan-Panda!

14:29.780 --> 14:31.992
HERE LIES CHIKARA

15:38.793 --> 15:40.253
DECEMBER 5TH

15:40.253 --> 15:42.007
TOKYO-JINBOCHO

15:47.769 --> 15:49.731
You really going in there alone?

15:49.731 --> 15:50.900
Y-Yeah.

15:50.900 --> 15:52.862
I think it'd be better if I went in with you-

15:52.862 --> 15:54.323
No, you see, um...

15:54.616 --> 15:57.789
Let's just say, you don't look the part
of a shojo manga artist.

15:57.789 --> 15:58.498
Huh?

15:58.749 --> 16:01.505
And you know, our goal here
is to win credibility, so yeah.

16:06.389 --> 16:08.894
I'm really sorry!
Just wait out here for me!

16:20.292 --> 16:22.797
Whoa... wow...

16:24.466 --> 16:28.684
Hello there. Sorry for the wait.
You're a first-timer, right?

16:29.101 --> 16:30.061
Oh, yes.

16:30.395 --> 16:32.901
All right.
Then let's see what you've got!

16:35.280 --> 16:37.785
"Undead Plus Unluck", huh?

16:37.785 --> 16:40.123
Oh, the "plus" is silent!

16:40.123 --> 16:41.543
Aah, okay.

16:51.354 --> 16:52.941
How long did this take you?

16:53.191 --> 16:55.320
Huh? Well, let's see...

16:56.280 --> 17:00.038
<i>I don't know the standard,
and I can't say it only took a day, either.</i>

17:00.330 --> 17:02.585
A-About a week.

17:02.752 --> 17:05.006
A week? You drew this in a week?

17:05.340 --> 17:06.718
Yes!

17:07.052 --> 17:11.812
OFF TODAY-PLEASE DON'T LOOK FOR ME
I only said that to make a good impression!
Manga artists of the world, forgive me!

17:12.855 --> 17:17.364
The composition is awfully refined...
All this at just 18, huh?

17:17.364 --> 17:19.285
That's the part Andy handled!

17:19.828 --> 17:22.457
The character art is also pretty good.

17:22.750 --> 17:23.919
Whuh?

17:24.336 --> 17:28.887
Of course, unlike your composition,
your line work and designs don't cut it at all.

17:28.887 --> 17:30.558
Your art style is too old school.

17:30.850 --> 17:33.606
And it seems to lack design sense.

17:33.606 --> 17:34.774
NO TASTE IN DESIGN!

17:35.818 --> 17:39.951
But it has charm.
I can, well... feel it.

17:40.201 --> 17:40.911
Huh?

17:41.329 --> 17:44.753
I can feel you really love the hero of this story.

17:45.003 --> 17:46.590
Did you base him on someone?

17:47.592 --> 17:50.890
Hah, of course you wouldn't have
a zombie boyfriend!

17:51.558 --> 17:56.860
Right... if someone like that existed,
I'd wind up falling for them.

17:59.448 --> 18:03.874
So do you want to submit this
to the contest? I think it'll place great.

18:03.874 --> 18:05.836
Oh! Yes, please do!

18:06.713 --> 18:11.890
Um... actually, I have a request, if you don't mind.

18:17.192 --> 18:18.904
Now it makes sense.

18:19.363 --> 18:22.620
Once you said you're a You-Me fan,
it all clicked.

18:22.620 --> 18:26.377
That manga is a unique one, too,
with its heavy use of sci-fi elements.

18:27.964 --> 18:31.429
Normally this isn't allowed,
but it's a special treat.

18:31.722 --> 18:34.476
Th-Then, you're really showing me
the raw manuscripts?

18:34.644 --> 18:39.571
Sure! Nowadays, we're all about digital manuscripts.
So chances like this are pretty rare.

18:41.115 --> 18:43.662
You ought to see the power
an analog manuscript holds.

18:44.329 --> 18:45.875
Now, let's see...

18:49.006 --> 18:49.716
Huh?

18:50.425 --> 18:52.930
Well, that's odd.
What's this writing?

18:52.930 --> 18:54.893
TO YOU, FROM ME

18:55.477 --> 18:56.938
Andy! It's in Japanese!

18:57.189 --> 18:58.107
Yeah.

18:58.107 --> 18:59.151
That seals it.

18:59.611 --> 19:02.909
You-Me is definitely a book of prophecy, Fuko.

19:05.163 --> 19:08.712
Um... You-Me has some rejected storylines, right?

19:09.672 --> 19:10.883
How do you know that?

19:11.217 --> 19:13.722
Huh? Oh, well, y'see...

19:14.139 --> 19:18.481
Anno-sensei has always excelled at story structure!

19:18.481 --> 19:23.115
So some awkward progression in the later parts
of the story stood out-I mean...

19:23.491 --> 19:26.831
Don't get me wrong,
it stayed great till the end, but...

19:28.042 --> 19:32.467
That's right! So you could tell!
We shelved three arcs!

19:32.677 --> 19:33.679
Three?

19:34.054 --> 19:35.724
<i>The Kohei's Betrayal arc.</i>

19:36.308 --> 19:37.770
UNBREAKABLE
<i>The Four Kings of the Four Season's arc.</i>

19:38.187 --> 19:40.275
And the Ando's Past arc.

19:41.528 --> 19:44.283
Both of you, get in contact
with Anno Un immediately!

19:44.617 --> 19:49.711
They intentionally left out details about the future!
I want those details and why they were withheld!

19:50.169 --> 19:53.969
Under most likely hasn't caught on to this intel.

19:54.303 --> 19:56.933
We'll seize it for ourselves
and gain the upperhand!

19:57.392 --> 20:03.404
I can dispatch other members if necessary!
I'll leave it to Andy to decide if he wants more members!

20:07.580 --> 20:12.047
B-But we don't even know where Anno-sensei is.

20:12.047 --> 20:15.219
Hello, Anno-sensei?
It's me, Tahioka.

20:16.221 --> 20:20.438
I know you prefer to stay silent,
so I'll cut to the point.

20:20.438 --> 20:25.532
The first matter is that the manuscripts you have
stored here might have been replaced.

20:26.033 --> 20:29.999
The other is that we need you to judge this month's contest.

20:30.249 --> 20:31.711
U-Um...

20:32.003 --> 20:36.220
For the first matter, I'll give you a report after
we've done some more investigating.

20:36.220 --> 20:38.015
As for the second,
are you available to judge?

20:38.015 --> 20:40.562
Um... would it be possible to speak with them?

20:40.896 --> 20:41.731
Huh?

20:44.361 --> 20:46.240
I can't do such a thing-

20:46.616 --> 20:48.119
Huh?

20:49.121 --> 20:50.289
Huh?

20:54.297 --> 20:55.341
Huh?

20:57.888 --> 20:59.433
Thank you very much.

21:00.769 --> 21:03.065
Hello, Anno-sensei.

21:03.984 --> 21:07.198
Nice to meet you.
My name is Fuko Izumo.

21:07.742 --> 21:13.252
Would you mind reading my manga?
I would appreciate it very much if you did.

21:13.879 --> 21:17.720
If it's too far for your convenience,
I don't mind coming to you.

21:19.932 --> 21:22.897
You're wasting your breath.
Anno-sensei doesn't speak to others.

21:23.565 --> 21:25.611
I've never even seen them before.

21:25.861 --> 21:26.780
Is it any good?

21:29.827 --> 21:32.207
If it's an interesting read,
then I'll meet with you.

21:32.833 --> 21:37.008
In five hours, come to the bench
at Stanley Park in Canada.

21:37.635 --> 21:39.346
Both of you together.

21:43.563 --> 21:46.653
Th-That's the first time I've heard their voice.

21:55.796 --> 22:00.012
MEMORIES OF FUKO IZUMO INSIDE
OF SHUEISHA HEADQUARTERS,

22:00.012 --> 22:02.016
17:00

22:02.016 --> 22:04.020
ERASED.

22:04.020 --> 22:09.030
TO BE CONTINUED

23:39.044 --> 23:39.670
PREVIEW

23:39.879 --> 23:43.636
<i>An autumn forest where red leaves fall...
that is the crossroads of fate.</i>

23:44.095 --> 23:47.561
<i>The unlucky girl and the undead man
finally reach this location.</i>

23:47.561 --> 23:51.611
ANNO UN
<i>Next episode of Undead Unluck,
Episode 20-Anno Un.</i>

23:51.694 --> 23:53.656
<i>In search of the greatest death ever.</i>
